@startuml learner-module-internal
' Ports-and-adapters inside the Learner Profiling module, as implemented at the end of Step 4.
' Dependencies point inwards only; the domain ring knows no framework.
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "competency.api (named interface)" {
  [CompetencyId]
  [CompetencyFrameworkId]
}

package "learner.api (named interface)" {
  [LearnerId]
}

package "domain" {
  [LearnerProfile\n(aggregate root)] as AGG
  [ProficiencyAssertion\n(entity, immutable state)] as PA
  [EvidenceRecord\n(append-only)] as EV
  [AttainedLevel\n(ordinal + framework code)] as LVL
  [AuthSubject\n(JWT sub, opaque)] as SUBJ
  [Confidence · DisplayName\nAssertionId · EvidenceType] as VO
  [LearnerProfileSummary\n(read model)] as SUM
  [LearnerProfileRepository\n(driven port)] as REPO
  [ConflictingFramework ·\nDuplicateProfile · NotFound] as EXC
}

package "domain.policy" {
  [LevelResolutionPolicy\n(domain service port)] as POL
  [HighestConfidenceResolutionPolicy\n(default)] as HCP
  [UnresolvableEvidenceException] as UEX
}

package "application" {
  [LearnerProfileService\n(transaction boundary)] as SVC
  [CreateLearnerProfileCommand\nRecordEvidenceCommand] as CMD
  [LearnerModuleConfiguration] as MCFG
}

package "infrastructure.web" {
  [LearnerProfileController\n/api/learners] as CTRL
  [LearnerWebMapper] as WMAP
  [ExceptionHandler -> RFC 9457] as EXH
  [Request / Response DTOs] as DTO
}

package "infrastructure.persistence" {
  [JpaLearnerProfileRepository] as JREPO
  [Profile · Assertion · Evidence\nJPA entities] as ENT
  [Spring Data + summary projection] as SD
}

CTRL --> SVC
CTRL --> WMAP
CTRL --> DTO
CTRL --> EXH
WMAP --> CMD
SVC --> CMD
SVC --> AGG
SVC --> REPO
SVC --> POL
SVC --> EXC
MCFG --> HCP
AGG --> LearnerId
AGG --> SUBJ
AGG --> PA
AGG --> VO
AGG --> POL
PA --> EV
PA --> LVL
PA --> CompetencyId
PA --> CompetencyFrameworkId
EV --> LVL
EV --> VO
HCP .up.|> POL
HCP --> UEX
JREPO .up.|> REPO
JREPO --> ENT
JREPO --> SD
SD --> SUM

note right of AGG
  Invariants inside the boundary:
  at most one assertion per competency
  (recordEvidence extends or opens);
  an assertion's framework is fixed
  once opened — conflicting evidence
  is rejected, not merged
end note

note bottom of PA
  ADR-019: CompetencyId and CompetencyFrameworkId
  are carried by value and never resolved — no query
  port, no cross-schema FK, no runtime call into
  Competency Modelling. The framework travels with
  the assertion because a level code is meaningless
  without it (ADR-018).
end note

note bottom of CTRL
  Ownership authorisation (ADR-015 Amendment 1) is
  enforced in two places, and neither is sufficient alone:

  (1) SecurityConfig (platform) — ordered chain rules
        GET /api/learners     -> hasAnyRole(EDUCATOR, ADMIN)
             /api/learners/** -> authenticated()
  (2) LearnerProfileService — ownership predicate against
        the loaded aggregate, via isOwnedBy(AuthSubject)

  The chain cannot see whose profile is requested, so it
  admits on authentication alone and the application layer
  decides. This controller resolves the caller's role to a
  single callerMayReadAny boolean and passes it inward;
  the learner module never sees the Role type, which lives
  in platform and which its module DAG forbids it to reach.

  Denial is 404, not 403, so a profile's existence is not
  disclosed. Insufficient *role* is still 403 from the
  chain, which reveals nothing about a specific resource.
end note

note right of POL
  ADR-018: resolution is a substitutable port, not a method
  on the aggregate. A lambda policy lets every aggregate
  invariant be tested without resolution arithmetic — the
  same seam ConformanceValidator gave CompetencyFramework.
  The default orders by confidence, then recency, then
  ordinal, then level code; the last tie-break is what makes
  the order total and consistent with AttainedLevel.equals.
end note

note bottom of SUBJ
  ADR-016: the caller's identity arrives as command data,
  extracted from the validated JWT by the controller and
  passed inward as an ordinary value. Nothing in the
  application or domain reads SecurityContextHolder — a
  rule the applicationStaysOutOfAdapters fitness function
  enforces — which is why the whole ownership matrix is
  testable with no security infrastructure at all.
end note

note bottom of JREPO
  ADR-020: relational tables, not a jsonb document.
  uq_assertion_profile_competency makes the aggregate's
  central invariant unviolatable at rest, discharging the
  trust assumption reconstitute() records. Evidence row ids
  are derived from (assertionId, seq) so re-saving updates
  in place instead of colliding with its own orphans.
end note
@enduml
